  "query_preview": "..Friday through Tuesday\n\nDeep-layer northwesterly flow behind the departing trough will \nquickly scour remaining low-level moisture by Friday morning. A \nsprawling 1028 mb surface high centered over the Canadian \nPrairies will build southeastward into the Midwest for the \nweekend, setting the stage for a prolonged stretch of quiet \nautumn weather.\n\nThermal profiles will start out chilly by Friday morning, with \n850 mb temperatures bottoming out near -2C to 0C. Weekend \nsensible weather will feature crisp daytime highs generally in \nthe low-to-mid 50s under mostly sunny skies. Efficient nocturnal\nradiational cooling--aided by slackening winds and a clear, dry\nboundary layer--will promote widespread frosty conditions, with\novernight lows dipping into the 30s across the area. \nAgricultural and late-season gardening interests should \nanticipate widespread frost/freeze potential Friday night and \nSaturday night.\n\nHeading into next week, ensemble consensus (GEFS/EPS) remains \nin strong agreement regarding an amplified synoptic pattern \nfeaturing persistent mid/upper-level ridging over the central \nCONUS, flanked by an anomalous cut-off low meandering across the\nDeep South/Gulf Coast region. This blocking configuration will \neffectively shut off poleward transport of Gulf moisture, \nlocking dry and tranquil conditions in place through mid-week. \nUnder continuous air mass modification and rising 500 mb \nheights, temperatures will gradually trend warmer, returning \ninto the 60s from Monday onward.",
